      "role": "user",
      "content": "so if the crystals are just re-arranging themselves, does that mean the bloom is basically just a sign that the tempering process failed and the structure is \"unstable\"? i'm trying to get a specific temp curve for my dark chocolate—could you give me a breakdown of the ideal melting, cooling, and reheating stages so i can make sure I'm hitting those stable crystals every time?",
